---
/** The caveat every page showing City votes carries. The City publishes no
 *  record of how each member voted, so these are read from its minutes, and
 *  readers should know exactly what that means before they rely on one. */
---
<div class="notice notice-warm">
  <p>
    <strong>How City votes are read.</strong> The City of North Vancouver
    doesn't publish a record of how each council member voted. Its minutes
    list who was present and, when a vote is not unanimous, name the people
    who opposed. So I count everyone present who isn't named as opposed as
    voting for, and anyone absent or out of the room as absent.
  </p>
  <p>
    That is a reading of the minutes, not a roll call. A person checks every
    vote against the minutes before it appears here, and each one links to
    the page it came from. Minutes are only final once council adopts them at
    a later meeting, and I mark the ones that haven't been adopted yet. If you
    find a vote shown wrongly, please{" "}
    <a href="mailto:corrections@northvanvotes.ca">tell me</a>.
  </p>
</div>
